<task id="022" project="spaarkeai-compose-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-01 baseline inversion in `SaveAsync` + drop `docx.js` export (E1 cutover — keystone)</title>
    <phase>2 E1</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>W2-E1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>002,003,020,021</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,frontend,docx,spe</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    THE KEYSTONE CUTOVER (FR-01). Invert the dirty-save baseline: on a dirty save the persisted
    document MUST be derived from the LOAD-TIME ORIGINAL OOXML, NOT a TipTap reconstruction. Remove
    `docx.js` from the export path — drop `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes` (and its caller `tipTapToDocxBytes`)
    from `utils/docxBridge.ts` so no dirty save routes through a full-document rebuild. Invert
    `ComposeService.SaveAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:315`) from "persist the client reconstruction" to
    "delta onto the retained original": resolve the baseline = the load-time SPE version by `versionId`
    (task 002 fetch), with the client-retained `state.docxBytes` as a same-session fast-path and a
    size-capped Redis cache (ADR-009, Tier-3) as fallback (FR-06); rebuild the edited paragraphs and
    splice them (task 020); synthesize the redline via the Docxodus adapter (task 021); write to SPE via
    the atomic `If-Match` path. This is an IRREVERSIBLE save-path cutover — execute the steps in order.
    GATED on task 003 (NFR-09 real-template hardening) passing before cutover.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack developer: .NET 8 (`ComposeService.SaveAsync`, Open XML, the SPE facade write) +
    React/TypeScript (`Spaarke.Compose.Components` save-path client, `docxBridge.ts`). Understands this
    is the single load-bearing inversion of R3 (design §8: "the save baseline becomes the retained
    original, and edits are deltas onto it") and that the R2 "Save regenerates .docx from editor"
    decision is being superseded (Path B).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A dirty save that persists a delta onto the retained load-time original: `docx.js` /
    `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes` removed from the export path; `ComposeService.SaveAsync` resolves the
    load-time baseline (version-by-`versionId` primary, client-bytes fast-path, Redis fallback), drives
    task 020's splice + task 021's comparer, and writes via the atomic `If-Match` SPE path. A save after
    editing a formatted doc no longer routes through `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes`; a through-the-wire test
    (authored in task 024) asserts untouched paragraphs match the original structurally/semantically;
    a save after a page refresh (client bytes gone) still applies the delta onto the correct load-time
    version. The clean-save passthrough path is unchanged.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §4 (E1 keystone), §4.3 (baseline = load-time SPE version by `versionId`; client fast-path;
      Redis fallback — S4), §8 (SAVE pipeline diagram; "drop docx.js export"), §11 (Path B — supersede
      the R2 "regenerate from editor" decision). Current dirty save (§2) rebuilds the whole `.docx` from
      TipTap JSON via `docx ^9.0.3` (`docxBridge.ts:208` `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes`), and `SaveAsync`
      (`ComposeService.cs:315`) treats those already-lossy bytes as an opaque baseline (re-applies
      annotations at `ComposeService.cs:358`). The clean-save passthrough (`state.docxBytes`) is already
      faithful — this task extends the faithful-baseline model from clean to dirty. All 6 spikes passed;
      the only pre-cutover residual is task 003 (real-template hardening), which GATES this cutover.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:315 — SaveAsync: invert to delta-onto-retained-original; resolve baseline (versionId primary / client-bytes fast-path / Redis fallback); drive the splice (020) + comparer (021); write via If-Match</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts:208 — REMOVE `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes` (docx.js export) and its caller `tipTapToDocxBytes` (:145); dirty save must not reconstruct the whole doc</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx — `triggerSave` baseline: send load-time original reference (versionId) + the paragraph-edit list instead of a client reconstruction</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:1107 — PushAnnotationsAsync download→annotate→replace + If-Match write; the reference save shape to generalize</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — task 020 splice orchestration + task 021 WmlComparer adapter (invoked here)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — task 002 version-content fetch (baseline by `versionId`, FR-06)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §4, §4.3, §8, §11 (Path B)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md FR-01, FR-06, NFR-07</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">`SpeFileStore` version-content fetch — the load-time baseline retrieval by `versionId` (FR-06 primary source).</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">NFR-09 real-template hardening gate — MUST pass before this cutover (a failure gates the delta-save cutover).</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">FR-02 edited-paragraph rebuild + splice — produces the spliced-edited document.</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">FR-03/FR-05 Docxodus WmlComparer adapter — synthesizes the redline from original vs spliced-edited.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-01">On a dirty save the persisted document MUST derive from the load-time original OOXML, NOT a TipTap reconstruction. `docx.js` is removed from the export path — a dirty save no longer routes through `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes`. MUST NOT reconstruct the whole doc from TipTap.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-06 / ADR-009 / ADR-015">Baseline = the load-time SPE version fetched by `versionId` (task 002). Client-retained `state.docxBytes` is a same-session fast-path; a size-capped Redis cache (Tier-3, document bytes) is the fallback. A save after a page refresh still applies the delta onto the correct load-time version.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / ADR Tension Path B">This supersedes the R2 project decision "Save regenerates `.docx` from editor" → "delta onto retained original." Cite the Path B supersession in the PR description (design §11): "R2 regenerate-from-editor superseded → delta onto retained original." Project-level decision amendment, not an ADR-doc change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">The version-content fetch + SPE write stay behind the `SpeFileStore` facade — no `Microsoft.Graph` types in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI internals; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-10">Client save-path fetches use `@spaarke/auth` (no ad-hoc token handling).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size; report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB. Verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Through-the-wire proof is required for this save-path change (authored as the task 024 seam slice test); unit-green ≠ done. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification (save orchestration stays in `Services/Compose/`; reuses SaveAsync/SpeFileStore seams) in the PR description.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Retained-original delta save inversion; SPE version-by-versionId baseline; Redis-first Tier-3 cache; client save-path (docxBridge / ComposeWorkspace); BFF hygiene</topic>
