    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Download→delta→If-Match write" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:1107">
        PushAnnotationsAsync fetches retained-original bytes, produces new bytes, and writes with an atomic If-Match etag — generalize this shape into the main dirty-save path.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Clean-save passthrough" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:315">
        SaveAsync already passes through faithful original bytes on a clean save — extend that faithful-baseline model to the dirty path.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Gate + context check">Confirm task 003 (NFR-09 real-template hardening) has PASSED — this cutover is gated on it. Confirm tasks 002/020/021 seams are available. Confirm `spaarkeai-compose-r2` is merged/frozen (CLAUDE.md coordination). Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load knowledge files + bff-extensions.md; state the Placement Justification + the Path B supersession note for the PR.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Server: implement baseline resolution">In `SaveAsync`, add baseline resolution: primary = load-time SPE version by `versionId` (task 002 fetch); fast-path = client-supplied `state.docxBytes` when present (same session); fallback = size-capped Redis cache of the load-time original (ADR-009 Tier-3). Return a clear error if no baseline can be resolved rather than falling back to a reconstruction.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Server: drive splice + comparer">Wire `SaveAsync` (dirty path) to: rebuild edited paragraphs + splice onto a copy of the resolved baseline (task 020), then synthesize the redline via the Docxodus adapter (task 021). Continue to apply AI redlines/comments via `DocxAnnotationWriter` (unchanged; task 023 verifies). Persist via the atomic `If-Match` SPE write.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Client: drop docx.js export">Remove `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes` (`docxBridge.ts:208`) and its caller `tipTapToDocxBytes` (:145). Update `ComposeWorkspace.triggerSave` to send the load-time original reference (versionId) + the paragraph-edit list (paraId-keyed) instead of a reconstructed `.docx`. Ensure the clean-save passthrough remains. Fetches via `@spaarke/auth`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify no reconstruction path remains">Grep the client for remaining references to `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes` / `tipTapToDocxBytes` / the `docx` export lib in the save path; confirm the dirty save no longer reconstructs. Build the shared lib (`npm run build`).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Build + verify server">Build BFF; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests (no regression). Run the Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check. (The through-the-wire fidelity proof is task 024.)</step>
    <step order="6" name="Size/CVE report + index">Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`. Update TASK-INDEX status; record the Path B supersession in the PR description.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (SaveAsync inverted to delta-onto-retained-original + baseline resolution)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts (docx.js export removed)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (triggerSave sends baseline reference + edit list)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan; Placement Justification; Path B supersession note for the PR</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A save after editing a formatted document no longer routes through `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes`; that function (and `tipTapToDocxBytes`) is removed from `docxBridge.ts` and no save path references docx.js reconstruction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On a dirty save, `SaveAsync` derives the persisted document from the load-time original OOXML (baseline resolved by `versionId`, with client-bytes fast-path / Redis fallback), then applies the splice + comparer delta — not a client reconstruction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A save after a page refresh (client `state.docxBytes` gone) still applies the delta onto the correct load-time version (FR-06 baseline retrieval).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The clean-save passthrough path is unchanged (still faithful).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`; the version fetch + write stay behind `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR description cites the Path B supersession of the R2 "regenerate from editor" decision (design §11).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; BFF + shared-lib builds green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

